# Elixir Koans - 05 Tuples

```elixir
import ExUnit.Assertions
```

## Tuples can contain different things

```elixir
assert {:a, 1, "hi"} == ___
```

## Tuples have a size

```elixir
assert tuple_size({:a, :b, :c}) == ___
```

## You can pull out individual elements

```elixir
assert elem({:a, "hi"}, 1) == ___
```

## You can change individual elements of a tuple

```elixir
assert put_elem({:a, "hi"}, 1, "bye") == ___
```

## You can also simply extend a tuple with new stuff

```elixir
assert Tuple.insert_at({:a, "hi"}, 1, :new_thing) == ___
```

## Add things at the end (by constructing a new tuple)

```elixir
{first, second} = {"Huey", "Dewey"}
extended = {first, second, "Louie"}
```

```elixir
assert extended == ___
```

## Or remove them

```elixir
assert Tuple.delete_at({:this, :is, :not, :awesome}, 2) == ___
```

## Turn it into a list in case you need it

```elixir
assert Tuple.to_list({:this, :can, :be, :a, :list}) == ___
```

